# Bake cache versioning

Disk caches live in `user://cache/` via [`scripts/world/bake_cache.gd`](scripts/world/bake_cache.gd). Full policy: [`docs/BAKE_CACHE.md`](docs/BAKE_CACHE.md).

When changing **packed binary layout** or **what a bake produces**, you must invalidate old blobs. Do **not** load incompatible cache bytes. Do **not** add silent migration/fallbacks unless the user explicitly asks.

| Change | Bump / update |
|--------|----------------|
| Atlas or sector pack fields/order/types | `BakeCache.FORMAT_VERSION` |
| LOD0 chunk pack (mesh/water/props/bridges) | `BakeCache.CHUNK_FORMAT_VERSION` |
| Atlas generator meaning / cell contract | `ContinentAtlas.SCHEMA_VERSION` |
| New config knobs that change sector/atlas content | `WorldConfig.content_hash()` |
| New knobs that change mesh/density only | `WorldConfig.mesh_content_hash()` |

Mismatch behaviour (already implemented): warn → cache miss → regenerate. Keep it that way.
